(window.RW_DISPLAY = window.RW_DISPLAY || {})["test04_1A"] = [{"id":"f7c02e89","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Cross-Text Connections","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Cross-Text Connections","passage":"Text 1 Films and television shows commonly include a long list of credits naming the people involved in a production. Credit sequences may not be exciting, but they generally ensure that everyone’s contributions are duly acknowledged. Because they are highly standardized, film and television credits are also valuable to anyone researching the careers of pioneering cast and crew members who have worked in the mediums. Text 2 Video game scholars face a major challenge in the industry’s failure to consistently credit the artists, designers, and other contributors involved in making video games. Without a reliable record of which people worked on which games, questions about the medium’s development can be difficult to answer, and the accomplishments of all but its best-known innovators can be difficult to trace.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Text 1","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Films and television shows commonly include a long list of credits naming the people involved in a production. Credit sequences may not be","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"exciting, but they generally ensure that everyone’s contributions are duly acknowledged. Because they are highly standardized, film and television","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"credits are also valuable to anyone researching the careers of pioneering cast and crew members who have worked in the mediums.","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Text 2","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Video game scholars face a major challenge in the industry’s failure to consistently credit the artists, designers, and other contributors involved","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"in making video games. Without a reliable record of which people worked on which games, questions about the medium’s development can be","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"difficult to answer, and the accomplishments of all but its best-known innovators can be difficult to trace.","indent":0}],"question":"Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 1 most likely respond to the discussion in Text 2?","choices":["By recommending that the scholars mentioned in Text 2 consider employing the methods regularly used by film and television researchers","By pointing out that credits have a different intended purpose in film and television than in the medium addressed by the scholars mentioned in Text 2","By suggesting that the scholars mentioned in Text 2 rely more heavily on credits as a source of information than film and television researchers do","By observing that a widespread practice in film and television largely prevents the kind of problem faced by the scholars mentioned in Text 2"]},{"id":"ac9a3a26","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"According to historian Vicki L. Ruiz, Mexican American women made crucial contributions to the labor movement during World War II. At the time, food processing companies entered into contracts to supply United States armed forces with canned goods. Increased production quotas conferred greater bargaining power on the companies employees, many of whom were Mexican American women: employees insisted on more favorable benefits, and employers, who were anxious to fulfill the contracts, complied. Thus, labor activism became a platform for Mexican American women to assert their agency.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined portion in the text as a whole?","choices":["It elaborates on a claim about labor relations in a particular industry made earlier in the text.","It offers an example of a trend in the World War II– era economy discussed earlier in the text.","It notes a possible exception to the historical narrative of labor activism sketched earlier in the text.","It provides further details about the identities of the workers discussed earlier in the text."],"underline":null,"underline_segments":["employees insisted on more","favorable benefits, and employers, who were anxious to fulfill the contracts, complied."]},{"id":"69a6d050","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"In the early 1800s, the Cherokee scholar Sequoyah created the first script, or writing system, for an Indigenous language in the United States. Because it represented the sounds of spoken Cherokee so accurately, his script was easy to learn and thus quickly achieved ______ use: by 1830, over 90 percent of the Cherokee people could read and write it.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["widespread","careful","unintended","infrequent"]},{"id":"be612a26","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"Recent measurements of the mass of the W boson (a subatomic particle) were notable not only for the mere fact that the particle’s mass differed from expectations but for the ______ of that difference: the measured mass of the W boson was seven standard deviations higher than predicted by the standard model of particle physics.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Recent measurements of the mass of the W boson (a subatomic particle) were notable not only for the mere fact that the particle’s mass","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"differed from expectations but for the ______ of that difference: the measured mass of the W boson was seven standard deviations higher than","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"predicted by the standard model of particle physics.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["cause","existence","implication","scale"]},{"id":"65406d2c","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"Dubautia carrii is a species in a family of plants known collectively as the silversword alliance, all of which grow only on the Hawaiian Islands. Members of this alliance exhibit an extraordinary range of phenotypes, with some species maturing into vines and others into shrubs and trees. All species in the alliance descended from a single ancestral tarweed plant that arrived on the islands around 5 million years ago. The tarweed’s descendants diversified into distinct species as they adapted to live in the wide variety of habitats found on the Hawaiian Islands.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Dubautia carrii is a species in a family of plants known collectively as the silversword alliance, all of which grow only on the Hawaiian Islands.","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Members of this alliance exhibit an extraordinary range of phenotypes, with some species maturing into vines and others into shrubs and trees.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"All species in the alliance descended from a single ancestral tarweed plant that arrived on the islands around 5 million years ago. The tarweed’s","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"descendants diversified into distinct species as they adapted to live in the wide variety of habitats found on the Hawaiian Islands.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?","choices":["To indicate the specific tarweed ancestor of all plants that grow on the Hawaiian Islands and explain why the plants have such varied physical characteristics","To describe the specific habitat where Dubautia carrii are found and identify other plants that share a common ancestor with them","To describe the silversword alliance and explain how the plant family became so varied","To advance the claim that all plants on the Hawaiian Islands are part of the silversword alliance and list possible ancestors of the plants that make up the alliance"]},{"id":"a5e747f0","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"Despite how ______ they may seem on first glance, the works of the philosopher Georg Hegel have proven to be quite influential. Readers who manage to penetrate Hegel’s frustratingly dense prose often find that his thrillingly original and profound ideas wind up shaping their own thinking.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Despite how ______ they may seem on first glance, the works of the philosopher Georg Hegel have proven to be quite influential. Readers who","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"manage to penetrate Hegel’s frustratingly dense prose often find that his thrillingly original and profound ideas wind up shaping their own","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"thinking.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["authoritative","opaque","empirical","facile"]},{"id":"f1c9d2c1","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Cross-Text Connections","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Cross-Text Connections","passage":"Text 1 Stage lighting theorist Adolphe Appia was perhaps the first to argue that light must be considered alongside all the various elements of a stage to create a single, unified performance. Researcher Kelly Bremner, however, has noted that Appia lacked technical expertise in the use of light in the theater. As a result of Appia’s inexperience, Bremner argues, Appia’s theory of light called for lighting practices that weren’t possible until after the advent of electricity around 1881. Text 2 Adolphe Appia was not an amateur in the practice of lighting. Instead, it is precisely his exposure to lighting techniques at the time that contributed to his theory on the importance of light. When working as an apprentice for a lighting specialist in his youth, Appia observed the use of portable lighting devices that could be operated by hand. This experience developed his understanding of what was possible in the coordination of elements on the stage.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Text 1","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Stage lighting theorist Adolphe Appia was perhaps the first to argue that light must be considered alongside all the various elements of a stage","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"to create a single, unified performance. Researcher Kelly Bremner, however, has noted that Appia lacked technical expertise in the use of light in","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"the theater. As a result of Appia’s inexperience, Bremner argues, Appia’s theory of light called for lighting practices that weren’t possible until","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"after the advent of electricity around 1881.","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Text 2","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Adolphe Appia was not an amateur in the practice of lighting. Instead, it is precisely his exposure to lighting techniques at the time that","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"contributed to his theory on the importance of light. When working as an apprentice for a lighting specialist in his youth, Appia observed the use","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"of portable lighting devices that could be operated by hand. This experience developed his understanding of what was possible in the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"coordination of elements on the stage.","indent":0}],"question":"Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to the claim about Appia’s level of technical expertise made by Bremner in Text 1?","choices":["Many lighting technicians dismissed Appia’s ideas about light on the stage.","Appia likely gained a level of technical expertise during his time as an apprentice.","Theater practitioners who worked with Appia greatly admired his work.","Appia was unfamiliar with the use of music and sound in theater."]},{"id":"81a3a607","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"In the Indigenous intercropping system known as the Three Sisters, maize, squash, and beans form an ______ web of relations: maize provides the structure on which the bean vines grow; the squash vines cover the soil, discouraging competition from weeds; and the beans aid their two “sisters” by enriching the soil with essential nitrogen.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["indecipherable","ornamental","obscure","intricate"]},{"id":"b62cb782","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"Culinary anthropologist Vertamae Smart-Grosvenor may be known for her decades of work in national public television and radio, but her book Vibration Cooking: or, the Travel Notes of a Geechee Girl is likely her most influential project. The 1970 book, whose title refers to Smart- Grosvenor’s roots in the Low Country of South Carolina, was unusual for its time. It combined memoir, recipes, travel writing, and social commentary and challenged notions about conventions of food and cooking. Long admired by many, the book and its author have shaped contemporary approaches to writing about cuisine.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Culinary anthropologist Vertamae Smart-Grosvenor may be known for her decades of work in national public television and radio, but her book","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Vibration Cooking: or, the Travel Notes of a Geechee Girl is likely her most influential project. The 1970 book, whose title refers to Smart-","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Grosvenor’s roots in the Low Country of South Carolina, was unusual for its time. It combined memoir, recipes, travel writing, and social","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"commentary and challenged notions about conventions of food and cooking. Long admired by many, the book and its author have shaped","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"contemporary approaches to writing about cuisine.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best describes the main idea of the text?","choices":["Smart-Grosvenor’s unconventional book Vibration Cooking: or, the Travel Notes of a Geechee Girl is an important contribution to food writing.","Smart-Grosvenor held many different positions over her life, including reporter and food writer.","Smart-Grosvenor’s groundbreaking book Vibration Cooking: or, the Travel Notes of a Geechee Girl didn’t receive the praise it deserved when it was first published in 1970.","Smart-Grosvenor was a talented chef whose work inspired many people to start cooking for themselves."]},{"id":"dc5edbf6","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"Microplastics are pieces of plastic that are smaller than a grain of rice. These small plastics can be found in large quantities in ocean waters. Ecologist Jessica Reichert and her team are studying the role reef-building corals have in capturing microplastics from ocean waters. Through research, her team has found that these corals may be storing up to 20 million kilograms of microplastics each year in their skeletons and tissues.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Microplastics are pieces of plastic that are smaller than a grain of rice. These small plastics can be found in large quantities in ocean waters.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Ecologist Jessica Reichert and her team are studying the role reef-building corals have in capturing microplastics from ocean waters. Through","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"research, her team has found that these corals may be storing up to 20 million kilograms of microplastics each year in their skeletons and","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"tissues.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","choices":["Ecologists are interested in learning more about how certain corals build large reefs.","Questions remain around the impact certain corals have on ocean ecosystems.","Microplastics are small pieces of plastic that can be found in ocean waters.","Ecologists predict that corals store large amounts of microplastics from ocean waters."]},{"id":"f27559d4","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Inferences","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Inferences","passage":"Volunteering, or giving time for a community service for free, is a valuable form of civic engagement because helping in a community is also good for society as a whole. In a survey of youths in the United States, most young people said that they believe volunteering is a way to help people on an individual level. Meanwhile, only 6% of the youths said that they think volunteering is a way to help fix problems in society overall. These replies suggest that ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Volunteering, or giving time for a community service for free, is a valuable form of civic engagement because helping in a community is also","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"good for society as a whole. In a survey of youths in the United States, most young people said that they believe volunteering is a way to help","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"people on an individual level. Meanwhile, only 6% of the youths said that they think volunteering is a way to help fix problems in society overall.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"These replies suggest that ______","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","choices":["many young people think they can volunteer only within their own communities.","volunteering may be even more helpful than many young people think it is.","volunteering can help society overall more than it can help individual people.","many young people may not know how to find ways to volunteer their time."]},{"id":"5d453dcc","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Voters’ Political Orientation, Level of Political Information, and Probability of Voting 100 90 Probability of voting (%) 80 70 60 50 40 30 20 10 0 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 Voters’ political orientation (1 = strong Democrat/liberal; 4 = independent; 7 = strong Republican/conservative) low information high information Economists Kerwin Kofi Charles and Melvin Stephens Jr. investigated a variety of factors that influence voter turnout in the United States. Using survey data that revealed whether respondents voted in national elections and how knowledgeable respondents are about politics, Charles and Stephens claim that the likelihood of voting is driven in part by potential voters confidence in their assessments of candidates — essentially, the more informed voters are about politics, the more confident they are at evaluating whether candidates share their views, and thus the more likely they are to vote.","passage_lines":[{"type":"chart","note":"[Graph: Voters’ Political Orientation, Level of Political Information, and Probability of Voting — not available here]"},{"type":"text","text":"Economists Kerwin Kofi Charles and Melvin Stephens Jr. investigated a variety of factors that influence voter turnout in the United States. Using survey data that revealed whether respondents voted in national elections and how knowledgeable respondents are about politics, Charles and Stephens claim that the likelihood of voting is driven in part by potential voters confidence in their assessments of candidates — essentially, the more informed voters are about politics, the more confident they are at evaluating whether candidates share their views, and thus the more likely they are to vote."}],"question":"Which choice best describes data in the graph that support Charles and Stephens’s claim?","choices":["At each point on the political orientation scale, high-information voters were more likely than low-information voters to vote.","Only low-information voters who identify as independents had a voting probability below 50%.","The closer that low-information voters are to the ends of the political orientation scale, the more likely they were to vote.","More voters strongly identified with a political party (orientations 1 and 7) than identified as independents (orientation 4)."]},{"id":"040583a5","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Banana Ripening Time at Different Temperatures with and without Ethylene Treatment 12 11 10 9 8 Time (days) 7 6 5 4 3 2 1 0 °C °C °C °C 14 16 18 20 Temperature (degrees Celsius) ethylene no ethylene A student is conducting an experiment to test the effect of temperature and ethylene treatment on the ripening speed of bananas. The student treated some bananas with ethylene while leaving others untreated, then allowed both types of bananas to ripen at one of four different temperatures. Comparing the data for bananas with and without ethylene, the student concluded that ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"chart","note":"[Graph: Banana Ripening Time at Different Temperatures with and without Ethylene Treatment — not available here]"},{"type":"text","text":"A student is conducting an experiment to test the effect of temperature and ethylene treatment on the ripening speed of bananas. The student treated some bananas with ethylene while leaving others untreated, then allowed both types of bananas to ripen at one of four different temperatures. Comparing the data for bananas with and without ethylene, the student concluded that ______"}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses data from the graph to complete the student’s conclusion?","choices":["20°C is the ideal temperature at which to store bananas to slow ripening time.","for those bananas that were not treated with ethylene, differences in temperature were not associated with absolute differences in ripening time.","bananas treated with ethylene ripen faster at 14°C and 16°C than at 18°C and 20°C.","ethylene was associated with a greater absolute change in ripening time at 14°C, 16°C, and 18°C than at 20°C."],"unusable":"missing graph"},{"id":"04bcb7a9","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"Xin Wang and colleagues have discovered the earliest known example of a flower bud in a 164-million-year-old plant fossil in China. The researchers have named the new species Florigerminis jurassica. They believe that the discovery pushes the emergence of flowering plants, or angiosperms, back to the Jurassic period, which occurred between 145 million and 201 million years ago.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Xin Wang and colleagues have discovered the earliest known example of a flower bud in a 164-million-year-old plant fossil in China. The","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"researchers have named the new species Florigerminis jurassica. They believe that the discovery pushes the emergence of flowering plants, or","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"angiosperms, back to the Jurassic period, which occurred between 145 million and 201 million years ago.","indent":0}],"question":"According to the text, how old was the fossil that Wang and colleagues discovered?","choices":["150 million years old","145 million years old","164 million years old","201 million years old"]},{"id":"33b1b285","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Founded in 1965 and originally established as a cultural extension of the United Farm Workers — a union representing many Mexican American agricultural workers at the time — the theater troupe El Teatro Campesino has achieved recognition as a source of inspiration for subsequent Chicano theater companies and as a contributor to the dramatic arts. In an article about the company, a theater historian posits that a significant stylistic influence on El Teatro’s early performances was the audience-mediated slapstick comedy of carpa theater, vaudeville-style shows popular in Mexico and the US Southwest in the 1920s and 30s.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Founded in 1965 and originally established as a cultural extension of the United Farm Workers—a union representing many Mexican American","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"agricultural workers at the time—the theater troupe El Teatro Campesino has achieved recognition as a source of inspiration for subsequent","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Chicano theater companies and as a contributor to the dramatic arts. In an article about the company, a theater historian posits that a significant","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"stylistic influence on El Teatro’s early performances was the audience-mediated slapstick comedy of carpa theater, vaudeville-style shows","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"popular in Mexico and the US Southwest in the 1920s and ’30s.","indent":0}],"question":"Which quotation from the article would best illustrate the theater historian’s claim?","choices":["“The company presented actos, short comedy sketches, that often relied on exaggerated physical humor to groups of agricultural workers, whose reactions — enthusiastic cheers of appreciation and, occasionally, loud boos of disapproval — promoted improvisation.”","“The company was focused on the reality of the present situation and discovered that humor was often found in that reality; consequently, comedy became a tool to convey social critique while entertaining and inspiring audiences.”","“The company relied heavily on satire, humor, and references to contemporary popular culture as well as a make-do aesthetic — often referred to as rasquache—that reflected not only the troupe’s limited financial resources but also its sociopolitical message.”","“The members of the company, which in addition to founder Luis Valdez consisted entirely of nonprofessional actors, traveled into farm fields, where they, with minimal props and costumes, performed comedy in the form of brief humorous vignettes.”"]},{"id":"f0864217","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Standard English · Form, Structure, and Sense","passage":"Rabinal Achí is a precolonial Maya dance drama performed annually in Rabinal, a town in the Guatemalan highlands. Based on events that occurred when Rabinal was a city-state ruled by a king, ______ had once been an ally of the king but was later captured while leading an invading force against him.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Rabinal Achí is a precolonial Maya dance drama performed annually in Rabinal, a town in the Guatemalan highlands. Based on events that","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"occurred when Rabinal was a city-state ruled by a king, ______ had once been an ally of the king but was later captured while leading an invading","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"force against him.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["Rabinal Achí tells the story of K’iche’ Achí, a military leader who","K’iche’ Achí, the military leader in the story of Rabinal Achí,","the military leader whose story is told in Rabinal Achí, K’iche’ Achí,","there was a military leader, K’iche’ Achí, who in Rabinal Achí"]},{"id":"863065c7","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Standard English · Form, Structure, and Sense","passage":"Legal scholars James Melton and Tom Ginsburg’s analysis of de jure judicial independence and its growth over decades ______ six constitutional features that enhance such independence, including judicial tenure and selection procedure. Albania’s constitution contains five of these features.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Legal scholars James Melton and Tom Ginsburg’s analysis of de jure judicial independence and its growth over decades ______ six constitutional","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"features that enhance such independence, including judicial tenure and selection procedure. Albania’s constitution contains five of these","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"features.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["are identifying","identify","have identified","identifies"]},{"id":"403d7bb5","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"According to Naomi Nakayama of the University of Edinburgh, the reason seeds from a dying dandelion appear to float in the air while ______ is that their porous plumes enhance drag, allowing the seeds to stay airborne long enough for the wind to disperse them throughout the surrounding area.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["falling,","falling:","falling;","falling"]},{"id":"a7c85001","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"Researchers Amit Kumar and Nicholas Epley investigated how ______ In a series of experiments conducted in 2022, they found that people performing small acts of kindness underestimated the positive effect their actions had on others.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["do people perceive acts of kindness.","do people perceive acts of kindness?","people perceive acts of kindness?","people perceive acts of kindness."]},{"id":"f1c5157d","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Standard English · Form, Structure, and Sense","passage":"Established in 1936 by African American novelist Richard Wright, ______ it would become a vital part of the creative movement known as the Chicago Black Renaissance.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Established in 1936 by African American novelist Richard Wright, ______ it would become a vital part of the creative movement known as the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Chicago Black Renaissance.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["the South Side Writers Group provided a valuable forum for Chicago writers to share ideas;","Chicago writers in the South Side Writers Group had a valuable forum for sharing ideas;","writers shared ideas at a valuable forum known as the South Side Writers Group in Chicago;","Chicago was where the South Side Writers Group provided a valuable forum for writers to share ideas;"]},{"id":"2bca654a","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Standard English · Form, Structure, and Sense","passage":"Forming extensive networks via mycorrhizal association — that is, a symbiotic relationship between plants and fungi — ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Forming extensive networks via mycorrhizal association—that is, a symbiotic relationship between plants and fungi—______","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["it is the entanglement of pine trees’ roots and the fungus Tricholoma matsutake’s fungal hyphae that makes nutrient transport possible.","the transport of nutrients is possible through the entanglement of pine trees’ roots and the fungus Tricholoma matsutake’s fungal hyphae.","nutrients can be transported through the entanglement of pine trees’ roots and the fungus Tricholoma matsutake’s fungal hyphae.","pine trees and the fungus Tricholoma matsutake can transport nutrients through their entangled tree roots and fungal hyphae."]},{"id":"f1d8550e","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Rhetorical Synthesis","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes: Jordan Bennett is a Mi’Kmaq visual artist. The Mi’Kmaq are a First Nations people in North America. Bennett’s paintings pay homage to traditional Mi’Kmaq craftsmanship and have been displayed in over 75 exhibitions. His 2017 exhibition Wije’wi was held at the Grenfell Art Gallery. His 2018 exhibition Ketu’elmita’jik was held at the Art Gallery of Nova Scotia. The student wants to emphasize the order in which two of Jordan Bennett’s exhibitions were held.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Jordan Bennett is a Mi’Kmaq visual artist.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"The Mi’Kmaq are a First Nations people in North America.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Bennett’s paintings pay homage to traditional Mi’Kmaq craftsmanship and have been displayed in over 75 exhibitions.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"His 2017 exhibition Wije’wi was held at the Grenfell Art Gallery.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"His 2018 exhibition Ketu’elmita’jik was held at the Art Gallery of Nova Scotia.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Jordan Bennett’s 2017 exhibition Wije’wi was followed a year later by his exhibition Ketu’elmita’jik.","Jordan Bennett’s paintings, some of which appeared in 2017 and 2018 exhibitions, pay homage to traditional Mi’Kmaq craftsmanship.","Mi’Kmaq visual artist Jordan Bennett has displayed his work in over 75 exhibitions, including Wije’wi and Ketu’elmita’jik.","Jordan Bennett’s 2018 exhibition Ketu’elmita’jik was held at the Art Gallery of Nova Scotia; another was held at the Grenfell Art Gallery."]},{"id":"63c73b50","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"In 2018, Kurt Luther and Vikram Mohanty created the web-based tool Civil War Photo Sleuth (CWPS). A user uploading an unknown Civil War soldier’s photograph to CWPS first tags the photo with all known information. ______ CWPS’s facial-recognition software analyzes twenty-seven different physical features and looks for matches to tagged images already in the database.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In 2018, Kurt Luther and Vikram Mohanty created the web-based tool Civil War Photo Sleuth (CWPS). A user uploading an unknown Civil War","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"soldier’s photograph to CWPS first tags the photo with all known information. ______ CWPS’s facial-recognition software analyzes twenty-seven","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"different physical features and looks for matches to tagged images already in the database.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Then,","In fact,","Likewise,","For example,"]},{"id":"a965c6ed","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"A turtle shell appears external to the animal, protecting its body like armor. ______ the shell is often incorrectly assumed to be an exoskeleton, a rigid outer casing like that of a crustacean or an insect, when in fact it is an endoskeleton, a part of the turtle’s internal bone structure, more akin to a spine or a pair of ribs.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"A turtle shell appears external to the animal, protecting its body like armor. ______ the shell is often incorrectly assumed to be an exoskeleton, a","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"rigid outer casing like that of a crustacean or an insect, when in fact it is an endoskeleton, a part of the turtle’s internal bone structure, more akin","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"to a spine or a pair of ribs.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["That being said,","However,","For instance,","Hence,"]},{"id":"56336696","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"When using sumac for dyeing cloth, textile artists first soak it in water to release its color. Then, they add the cloth to the dyebath and simmer it for hours, perhaps even days. ______ they will remove the cloth, at which point it will have turned a vibrant red color.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"When using sumac for dyeing cloth, textile artists first soak it in water to release its color. Then, they add the cloth to the dyebath and simmer it","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"for hours, perhaps even days. ______ they will remove the cloth, at which point it will have turned a vibrant red color.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Nevertheless,","Likewise,","Eventually,","In other words,"]},{"id":"0fd4df40","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"The Alaska Native Language Archive (ANLA) is known for its impressive audio collection. ______ the ANLA has more than 5,000 audio recordings of Native Alaskan languages dating as far back as 1943.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The Alaska Native Language Archive (ANLA) is known for its impressive audio collection. ______ the ANLA has more than 5,000 audio recordings","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"of Native Alaskan languages dating as far back as 1943.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["In fact,","After,","Regardless,","Instead,"]},{"id":"30438650","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"Jhumpa Lahiri’s story collection Interpreter of Maladies features multiple stories about romantic relationships. In “This Blessed House,” newlyweds argue over whether to replace items left by the previous owners of their new home. ______ in “A Temporary Matter,” a husband and wife attempt to rekindle their relationship during a four-night blackout.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Jhumpa Lahiri’s story collection Interpreter of Maladies features multiple stories about romantic relationships. In “This Blessed House,”","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"newlyweds argue over whether to replace items left by the previous owners of their new home. ______ in “A Temporary Matter,” a husband and","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"wife attempt to rekindle their relationship during a four-night blackout.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Granted,","For example,","Likewise,","Hence,"]}];
